    "methodology_note": "Source: macro_data.event_calendar (ADR 0004) populated by the economic-releases playbook per ADR 0008 (Bloomberg ticker 'NFP TCH Index').  Surprise is the EXACT IDENTITY ``actual \u2212 consensus_median`` (in thousands of jobs) \u2014 the ingestion layer intentionally leaves event_calendar.surprise NULL (ADR 0008 \u00a72) so the primitive layer carries the identity with the P12 disclosure on the wire (Bloomberg reports the same number; this primitive materialises a desk-recognised identity, NOT recomputed).  PRIOR-MONTH REVISIONS \u2014 the well-known NFP caveat.  Each NFP release re-states the prior month's actual via ``revised_prior``; these revisions can be material (sometimes larger than the headline surprise itself).  This series carries the AS-RELEASED surprise \u2014 it does NOT retroactively adjust prior surprise outputs when a revision arrives.  A revision-adjusted surprise primitive is a documented follow-up.  Scope: bounded by the ECO_RELEASE_DT_LIST release-date window (~1.5 years history + forward scheduled) per ADR 0008 \u00a76 / TD #28b \u2014 releases pre-dating that window return honest absence."
